G24 spike: battery levers and the Settings look (Author, 2026-11-20 to 2026-11-21)
=====================================================================================

Purpose: measure every doubt before the G24 ledger row is written (owner: "spike all doubts b4").
Device: LAB-STICK-1 (StickS3). Raw files: $GUARDIAN_STORE/evidence-raw/<dir>/ (sha256 below).

Images (throwaway diagnostic build, branch spike/power-exp, never merged; TUNE key pexp.mode, letters act
only on battery while the screen is Dark; the BATTRUN segment's dim_pct carries the mode as 200+mode):
  guardian-20261120-150740-pexp   modes A..F, P, I, S2 probe, S3 restart cycles
  guardian-20261120-222754-pexp   adds mode 8 = G (every lever at once, see below)
  guardian-20261121-103138        delivery image put back afterwards (main tree with the G23 silence log)
All installed over USB with esptool after a MAC check; every region hash-verified; same partition table.

1. Unused parts (S2, one probe read, MEASURED, 2026-11-20 16:00)
   PM1 PWR_CFG 0x06 = 0x17: green status LED lit, 5 V boost (Grove/Hat/IR supply) off, LDO, DCDC, charging on.
   PM1 GPIO_OUT 0x11 = 0x04: LCD/audio rail on, speaker amp off.
   G46 (IR TX gate): output disabled, low. Codec ES8311 answers and is powered down (its rail is shared with
   the LCD, so the microphone loses power only when the LCD rail is cut).

2. Radio stop/restart (S3, on USB, 100 cycles of 10 s listen / 5 s off, MEASURED)
   radio_offs=100 radio_ons=100 radio_fail=0; 4 cycles without frame plus lock inside the 10 s listen.
   Resume to first accepted frame: avg 3469 ms, max 8837 ms. Relock: avg 3567 ms over 96.
   On the G image overnight (380 cycles of 10 s / 50 s): radio_fail=0, rail_fail=0, pm_fail=0;
   resume avg 2893 ms, relock avg 2985 ms at the +10 min check.

3. Lever segments (charge 1, 20 min each, dark phase only, MEASURED; mV/h = mV/10min x 6)
   seg  mode                 start mV   mV/h
   1    A today              4171       444
   2    P unused parts off   3843       354
   3    A today              3658       168
   4    B P + radio off      3572        66
   5    A today              3551       282   then the 20 % floor (deep sleep)
   Reading: the discharge curve swamps 20-minute slope segments (A alone: 444, 168, 282). Radio off is the
   only lever clearly above that noise; P shows no separable saving. Modes C and D never ran (the floor came
   first). Decision: battery hours come from full drains only.

4. Full drains (MEASURED, from full to the 20 % floor, awake minutes from BATTRUN)
   Always listening, today's image (G23 soak and sheet A, 2026-11-20): 2 h 05 min to 2 h 08 min.
   G = listen 10 s / off 50 s + status LED off + IR TX held low + LCD rail cut while dark + IMU low-power
       + 80 MHz light sleep while the radio is off (2026-11-20 23:29 to 2026-11-21 06:4x):
       BATTRUN minutes=434 (awake), start 4163 mV, floor 3447 mV, sleeps=2, asleep_s=10577,
       seg1 A 474 s (the first poll set the mode), seg2 G 24208 s, dark 10 mV/10min over 23622 s.
       Result: about 7 h 14 min, a little more for G alone (its first 8 minutes ran A).
   Ratio G / always: about 3.4.

5. Detection cost of listening 10 s in every 60 s (worked, docs/G23-delivery.md section 11.4)
   An alert can be up to about 50 s late; a short burst entirely inside an off period is missed;
   "No fresh data" (29 s) must not show for the planned off periods.

6. Open
   One brownout reset on USB at about 3600 mV while charging (2026-11-21 09:51, G image, 10 min after a
   floor wake). Cause UNKNOWN. No earlier reset=brownout in any record (G16 to G24). Watched on the
   delivery image.
   Silence lock losses (G23 section 12): cause UNKNOWN; next step is a count of the lock network's frames by
   subtype during a gap.
   Not measured: listen 10 s / off 20 s with every lever; backlight levels while lit.

